onfidence of the fantastic production  in the long run  back in april rawson could be seen  asking the community of the make and  model of the dz helicopter  something that most probably wouldn't  care about but it's super awesome to see  the detail he's looking into  also in may he responded to someone  asking of the possibility of cosplayers  to be included in the film as extras  his response  considered doable and planned  details to follow  i haven't yet spoken to the guy yet but  based on his interactions with the  community and the feedback i had from  fellow division enthusiast born diesel  he sounds bloody awesome  given that he's talking about the  possibility of using cosplay community  members in the film maybe he'd be keen  on some other community input  i know i'm a man in his mid-thirties  with a dead body to suit but i have a  stunning resemblance to aaron kina  and a voice that i've been told aligns  well with the division story  maybe i could be a malfunctioning isaac  struggling with a language translation  oh bro there's lots of angry dudes over  there  cheers  damn it someone started petition for me  let's make this happen  the division heartlands without spoiling  too much is looking to be a new  stand-alone battle royale-ish type game  i haven't tried it myself but from what  i've seen it could hold some promise of  a decent game time will tell  and then of course we can't forget about  the acclaimed crossover that the  division has had with xdefiant where two  of the hostile factions make an  appearance  some of you may already be aware of my  thoughts behind this one if you watch  the video yeah i'll put the link there  but  be warned it was certainly a different  type of content for me  while all of these additions to the  division universe are cool most of us  are still left wondering what is  happening to the core game of the series  the last update we were given was a  message from almost six months ago  in the next major update we're looking  to bring in a game mode that's entirely  new to the franchise  along with the game mode we are  investigating new ways to progress your  agent with an emphasis on increasing  build variety and viability  we will be revealing more about what  lies ahead as the update gets closer  the development of this new update is  still in its early stages and will take  several months to complete as a result  our next major update is currently  scheduled for release late 2021 at its  earliest we will be taking this time to  make sure we bring a meaningful change  to the game  given that we're nearing the end of 2021  and we've still heard nothing people  understandably are starting to get  impatient  for a live service game updates are  usually provided far more frequently  than what we're seeing here  or at the very least there would be open  lines of communication like we used to  have with the state of the game  whether you liked it or hated it it was  still good to see the studio investing  this time into communicating with the  fans of the game  so the big question on everyone's mind  right now is what are the future plans  for the game  if any  we know massive entertainment are  working heavily on avatar and star wars  projects  the majority of people in the know  expected them to either be shutting down  the division or passing it off to  another ubisoft studio  but the announcement six months ago said  no  there is still more to come  however we didn't see the division at e3  this year and there wasn't even anyone  from the division community who was  nominated as one of the star players  it can be easy to blame it on the world  by pandemic and i'd say this definitely  had a big impact initially but games  like destiny and warframe seem to be  well back on track for new content  releases  even outriders and they don't even  consider their product a live service  game  [Music]  the division seems to be a bit of a  weird one for ubisoft  it's no secret that the divis